IMPORT daydate

-- Fatal Accidents Act 1959 (WA) -- the date arithmetic the baseline needs, kept in one small module so that the
-- daydate library is imported once. Every other module of this encoding imports this one, not daydate.

§ `Fatal Accidents Act 1959 -- dates`

-- A date written day, month, year (for the cases file, which does not import daydate).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS Date d m y

-- s 9(1): "within 6 months after the death of the deceased person". The period ends on the day of the month 6 months on
-- that has the death's day number; where that month is shorter, on its last day (daydate's `add months` clamps). The
-- Interpretation Act 1984 rules on reckoning time are borrowed and not encoded beyond this.
GIVEN death IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the 6 months after` death MEANS `add months` death 6

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or before` b IF Day a AT MOST Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls after` b IF Day a GREATER THAN Day b

-- The number of days from a to b (for the regulative rule, whose WITHIN counts days from the death).
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` a `to` b MEANS Day b MINUS Day a

-- Schedule 2 cl 1(a)(ii): "had been living on that basis with the deceased for at least 2 years immediately before the
-- deceased died". Two years from the start fall on the same day and month two years on (29 February clamps to 28).
GIVEN start IS A DATE, death IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `at least 2 years run from` start `to` death IF
    Day (`add months` start 24) AT MOST Day death
